triggers.WrenbowHelper/ScrambleRubiksCubeTrigger.placements.description.scramble_rubiks_cube_trigger=Applies a configurable amount of random turns to a Rubiks Cube state
triggers.WrenbowHelper/ScrambleRubiksCubeTrigger.attributes.description.cubeName=Cube state identifier to pair to
triggers.WrenbowHelper/ScrambleRubiksCubeTrigger.attributes.description.scrambleLength=How many turns to apply
triggers.WrenbowHelper/ScrambleRubiksCubeTrigger.attributes.description.doOnce=Delete this trigger after applying a scramble

# Feather Controller
entities.WrenbowHelper/FeatherController.placements.name.feather_controller=Feather Controller
entities.WrenbowHelper/FeatherController.attributes.description.highFlySpeed=The speed that the player will approach when traveling in the input direction
entities.WrenbowHelper/FeatherController.attributes.description.turnFlySpeed=The speed that the player will have while sharply turning
entities.WrenbowHelper/FeatherController.attributes.description.lowFlySpeed=The speed that the player will have when not holding any inputs
entities.WrenbowHelper/FeatherController.attributes.description.octalAnalog=Snaps analog angles to their closest octal direction
entities.WrenbowHelper/FeatherController.attributes.description.featherHyper=Allows for hypers to be performed out of feather state
entities.WrenbowHelper/FeatherController.attributes.description.trueFeatherSuper=Allows for supers to be performed out of feather state
entities.WrenbowHelper/FeatherController.attributes.description.trueFeatherWallBounce=Allows for wallbounces to be performed out of feather state
entities.WrenbowHelper/FeatherController.attributes.description.noStartSlowdown=Removes the initial slowdown period when entering feather state
entities.WrenbowHelper/FeatherController.attributes.description.noFeatherBoost=Removes the initial boost given when you finish transforming in feather state
entities.WrenbowHelper/FeatherController.attributes.description.allowPickup=Lets you pick up holdables while in feather state
entities.WrenbowHelper/FeatherController.attributes.description.allowThrowing=Lets you throw holdables while in feather state\nDoes not necessarily require allowPickup

# Line Of SIght Eye
entities.WrenbowHelper/LineOfSightEye.placements.name.line_of_sight_eye=Line Of Sight Eye
entities.WrenbowHelper/LineOfSightEye.placements.description.line_of_sight_eye=Activates a flag based on whether it has a line of sight to an entity\nCan also allow another entity to be the point of vision, and can look for a list of entities
entities.WrenbowHelper/LineOfSightEye.attributes.description.entityFrom=Entity used as the start point for line of sight\nSupports "self", "player", or an arbitrary entity's ID number
entities.WrenbowHelper/LineOfSightEye.attributes.description.entityTo=Entity(ies) used as the end point for line of sight\nSupports "self", "player", or an arbitrary entity's ID number
entities.WrenbowHelper/LineOfSightEye.attributes.description.flag=Flag to set while line of sight is detected
entities.WrenbowHelper/LineOfSightEye.attributes.description.flagIf=If a flag is given, it must be true to check line of sight
entities.WrenbowHelper/LineOfSightEye.attributes.description.maxRange=Detection range in pixels
entities.WrenbowHelper/LineOfSightEye.attributes.description.solids=If true, allows for line of sight to be blocked by solids\nThis includes both solidtiles and solid entities\nNote that the solidtile collision check can have weird edge cases
entities.WrenbowHelper/LineOfSightEye.attributes.description.lightBlockers=If true, allows for line of sight to be blocked by entities with a LightOcclude component\nIntended to allow entities such as doors and trapdoors to block vision
entities.WrenbowHelper/LineOfSightEye.attributes.description.drawSprite=Whether to show the eye sprite ingame\nRecommended to disable if not checking vision from self